<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Eureka attrib profit halves, posts div.</title>
<headline>Eureka attrib profit halves, posts div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre non-operating   63.4	  vs 63.3</p>
<p>    - post non-operating  63.4	  vs 144.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 25.0	  vs none</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   1.52	  vs 3.47</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   2.04	  vs 2.30</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.52	  vs 0.78</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.84	  vs 0.64</p>
<p>    Turnover		  15.40	 vs 16.49</p>
<p>Div payable Dec 20</p>
<p>on register Dec 13</p>
<p>Full name: Eureka Industrial Ltd</p>
<p>    Non-operating items   none	  vs 1.95</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said earnings should be maintained in the second half, barring unforeseen circumstances. Eureka was seeking alternative investment avenues, they said, but until found no substantial change in performance is expected, they said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
